      "date": "2026-07-27 22:07:11.000000000",
      "message": "Patch Set 4:\n\n(8 comments)\n\nAI code review results below, please doublecheck\n\nMostly good, minor comments inline. I replayed all 21 moved checks with gen_compat.py against real include/linux headers from v4.18, v5.4, v5.14, v6.1, v6.4, v6.6, v6.8, v6.9, v6.10 through v6.18, plus CentOS Stream 9 and 10, and every check flips at the same kernel version as the autoconf test it replaces, with the same macro definitions on both branches. So the functional side of the move looks correct; the comments below are about accuracy of the recorded upstream commits, one brittle match string, and the commit message list.",
